DMB : bidirectional full async barrier

DSB : all of DMB + stops instruction pipeline until memory effects have completed

ISB : flushes instruction cache such that following instructions wont hit out of it


3 types of memory normal/device/strongly ordered (really confusing) 

for all purposes consider normal and it uses weak consistency. adding a DMB
provides sequential consistency.

